        "note": "A radar gives a square root of a sum of squares. A pendulum turns with a sine. Neither is a matrix."
      },
      {
        "id": "the-line",
        "label": "A straight line at one place",
        "focus": [
          "jacob"
        ],
        "note": "The derivative of the model at the place the state stands now takes the place of the matrix."
      },
      {
        "id": "which-is-which",
        "label": "The state goes through the truth",
        "focus": [
          "truef",
          "cov"
        ],
        "note": "The true function moves the state. Only the uncertainty goes through the straight line."
      },
      {
        "id": "the-weakness",
        "label": "Where the line is wrong",
        "focus": [
          "bend"
        ],
        "note": "A line laid against a model that bends sharply is wrong a little way off, and the filter cannot know it."
      }
    ]
  },
