  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it works out",
      "items": [
        "F is the derivative of f at x, and H the derivative of h at x",
        "x = f(x, u), and P = F*P*F' + Q",
        "x = x + K*(y - h(x)), with K from H as the plain filter uses C"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Which goes through what",
      "items": [
        "The state goes through the TRUE function, bending as the model bends",
        "Only the uncertainty goes through the straight line",
        "Getting that the wrong way round is the usual fault"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Where it fails",
      "items": [
        "A straight line laid against a model that bends sharply is wrong a little way off",
        "The filter has no way to know that it is wrong",
        "Where the bend is severe, ukf answers without any derivative at all"
      ]
    }
  ]
